/playwright-report
/test-results
/.state

# Run scratch is ignored. Upload fixtures are not, and conflating the two is what reddened CI: with
# `/data/data-transfer/*.csv` ignored, a fresh checkout had no CSVs to upload and the data-transfer
# spec died on `ENOENT .../data/data-transfer/products.csv` before it reached a single assertion.
#
#   /test-data/runtime.json     a data bag one fixture writes for another to read; only this file
#                               lives in test-data/, the suite never reads it as an input, and it is
#                               rewritten on every run. Ignoring it is right.
#
# `data/data-transfer/*.csv` are *inputs*: the six CSVs the import cases upload, and nothing
# regenerates them, so they stay tracked. They are not read-only, though, and the difference matters
# to whoever runs this suite next: `updateCsv()` and `updateCsvProductId()` in
# `pages/settings/DataTransferPage.ts` rewrite the `person_id`, `organization_id` and `product`
# columns in place with ids read from the instance under test. A local run therefore leaves the
# tracked copies modified — do not commit that, restore it with
# `git checkout -- packages/Webkul/Admin/tests/e2e-pw/data/data-transfer/`.
#
# Deliberately not `/data/`: `data/images/` holds twelve fixture images the specs attach, and those
# are read-only inputs worth tracking.
#
# `.state/` needs no entry of its own -- `/.state` above already covers it.
/test-data/runtime.json
